{{!--
    The opening-titles player (foundry/opening-titles.mjs#raiseCurtain): a
    black curtain the moment the GM starts the titles, then each video of the
    press in turn (the chosen cut, then the episode's title card), full
    screen, above everything; at the end it fades out onto the episode's
    first scene.

      video   one element for every part; its source is set by the adapter
              (playPart) only after every listener is attached, so no error
              can slip past unheard.
      status  "Loading…", shown only while data-state="loading" (a video
              starting, or the scene still being drawn behind the curtain).
      gate    shown only while data-state="blocked": the browser would not
              start video with sound without a click, so here is the click.
              Its label names the part it would play.
      skip    always on screen. Skip or Escape skips what is playing in one
              press.

    data-state is written by the adapter: "curtain" before anything plays,
    then core/opening-titles.mjs's overlayStep for each video. Nothing on this
    screen blinks or pulses, since one of the two cuts promises no flashing at
    all. Must render exactly ONE top-level element.
--}}
<div class="bi-opening" data-state="loading" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="{{label}}">
    <video class="bi-opening__video" playsinline preload="auto"></video>
    <p class="bi-opening__status" aria-live="polite">{{loading}}</p>
    <div class="bi-opening__gate">
        <button type="button" class="bi-opening__play"><i class="fa-solid fa-play" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span class="bi-opening__play-label">{{play}}</span></button>
        <p class="bi-opening__gate-hint">{{playHint}}</p>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="bi-opening__skip" aria-label="{{skipHint}}">{{skip}} <kbd class="bi-opening__key">Esc</kbd></button>
</div>
